date: 2026-06-05T16:40:21-04:00
---

The Magical Crimes Convox is a department within the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]] devoted to solving the unexplained and the weird when they negatively impact the [[Iridescent Host|Host's]] people. Some cases they've worked on previously have included a mysterious curse originating from the [[Verdant Expanse]] and an everlasting rain from excessive [[Phenomena/Augury|augury]].

The convox is headquartered at 33 Rook's Crossing in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]].

Its deputy director is Major-Chaplain [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Ewan McFoster|Ewan McFoster]], who speaks for the convox in public. He blamed the endless rain that fell over [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] on an illegal augur. The Church reimburses the travel of its investigators.

Three of its members, [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Mickey Ironroots|Mickey Ironroots]], [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Cedric Corot|Cedric Corot]], and [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Krod Snodman|Krod Snodman]], worked the curse that left forty-eight dead in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], dried to husks in their beds. The trail ran through [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford|Wrenford]] into the [[Verdant Expanse]], where the three refused a [[Bestiary/Fey|court of fey]]'s offer to end the curse at the price of entering their Lady's court, and killed the court's leaders. That did not end the curse.

The case turned on [[Phenomena/Feyrock|Feyrock]], a stone bought and sold only by those wealthy enough to afford it. A Feyrock necklace from [[People/Lyric Burke|Lyric Burke]]'s house led through [[Org/Crystal's Rock|Crystal's Rock]] to [[Org/Guren and Guren/People/Amos Guren|Amos Guren]], who had bought a piece from a bandaged man in a black raiment, and from there to [[People/Anthony|Anthony]], found dead in his apartment in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Gullet/index|Gullet]] above a ritual circle, half-turned to stone, and to the [[Phenomena/Gloaming Codex|Gloaming Codex]] itself.
